Subject: [PATCH] staging: wire in the prima WLAN driver

The Wi-Fi of the WCNSS Pronto core is driven by Qualcomm's prima, which was
never part of this tree: the Xperia X has a Broadcom chip instead. As for the
3.10 kernel (../kernel/patches/0009), tools/setup-kernel.sh fetches it, here
from the LineageOS kernel for MSM8953 devices, 4.9.227 like this one, and this
wires it into drivers/staging. The WCNSS core driver it works with is already
in the tree, in drivers/soc/qcom/wcnss.
---
--- drivers/staging/Kconfig
+++ drivers/staging/Kconfig
@@ -106,4 +106,6 @@
 
 source "drivers/staging/vc04_services/Kconfig"
 
+source "drivers/staging/prima/Kconfig"
+
 endif # STAGING
--- drivers/staging/Makefile
+++ drivers/staging/Makefile
@@ -42,3 +42,4 @@
 obj-$(CONFIG_KS7010)		+= ks7010/
 obj-$(CONFIG_GREYBUS)		+= greybus/
 obj-$(CONFIG_BCM2708_VCHIQ)	+= vc04_services/
+obj-$(CONFIG_PRONTO_WLAN)	+= prima/
